# signing key — a leak lets anyone sign a mod as you
*.biprivatekey
keys/*.biprivatekey

# build output
build/out/
native/build/
# THE @Mod FOLDERS THEMSELVES ARE NOT IGNORED, and that is deliberate.
#
# @OpenZone_Radio/ used to be listed here, which hid the whole folder from
# git -- and with it mod.cpp, which is SOURCE, not output: it carries the
# mod name, author, version and the description a server owner reads in the
# launcher. Ignoring a directory also stops git descending into it, so an
# "!@OpenZone_Radio/mod.cpp" exception would not have worked either.
#
# The packed result is still ignored: *.pbo below covers it wherever it
# lands, which is all that needs ignoring.
*.pbo
*.bisign
*.log
*.RPT

# local
.compile-check-profile/
.dayz-mcp/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# машинний профіль MCP: шляхи цієї машини, не комітиться
dayz-mcp.local.toml
